13011,45],[18011006,18011007,41],[46002016,46002016,36],[19025014,19025014,32],[30003007,30003007,30],[40011027,40011030,25],[55003016,55003016,25]],"xn":26}},"people":[{"id":"israel_682","name":"Israel","also":"","summary":"One who follows on another’s heels; supplanter, (Gen. 25:26; 27:36; Hos. 12:2-4), the second born of the twin sons of Isaac by Rebekah. He was born probably at Lahai-roi, when his father was fifty-nine and Abraham one hundred and fifty-nine years old.","verses":1009,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[1,13]},{"id":"moses_2108","name":"Moses","also":"","summary":"Drawn (or Egypt. mesu, “son;” hence Rameses, royal son). On the invitation of Pharaoh (Gen. 45:17-25), Jacob and his sons went down into Egypt.","verses":774,"father":"Amram","mother":"Jochebed","v":[1,2]},{"id":"moab_2103","name":"Moab","also":"Moabitess, Moabitish, Moabites","summary":"Used to denote the people of Moab (Num. 22:3-14; Judg. 3:30; 2 Sam. 8:2; Jer. 48:11, 13).","verses":149,"father":"Lot","mother":"Daughter of Lot - Older","v":[1]},{"id":"pharaoh_2331","name":"Pharaoh","also":"","summary":"The Pharaoh of the Exodus was probably Menephtah I., the fourteenth and eldest surviving son of Rameses II. He resided at Zoan, where he had the various interviews with Moses and Aaron recorded in the book of Exodus.","verses":138,"father":"","mother":"","v":[2]},{"id":"sihon_2739","name":"Sihon","also":"","summary":"Striking down. The whole country on the east of Jordan, from the Arnon to the Jabbok, was possessed by the Amorites, whose king, Sihon, refused to permit the Israelites to pass through his territory, and put his army in array against them.","verses":34,"father":"","mother":"","v":[7]},{"id":"og_2238","name":"Og","also":"","summary":"Gigantic, the king of Bashan, who was defeated by Moses in a pitched battle at Edrei, and was slain along with his sons (Deut. 1:4), and whose kingdom was given to the tribes of Reuben and Gad and half the tribe of Manasseh (Num. 21:32-35; Deut. 3:1-13).","verses":22,"father":"","mother":"","v":[7]},{"id":"manasseh_1928","name":"Manasseh","also":"Manasses","summary":"The elder of the two sons of Joseph. He and his brother Ephraim were afterwards adopted by Jacob as his own sons (48:1).","verses":109,"father":"Joseph","mother":"Asenath","v":[8]},{"id":"abraham_58","name":"Abraham","also":"Abram","summary":"Father of a multitude, son of Terah, named (Gen. 11:27) before his older brothers Nahor and Haran, because he was the heir of the promises. Till the age of seventy, Abram sojourned among his kindred in his native country of Chaldea.","verses":277,"father":"Terah","mother":"","v":[13]},{"id":"isaac_616","name":"Isaac","also":"","summary":"The only son of Abraham by Sarah. He was the longest lived of the three patriarchs (Gen. 21:1-3).","verses":123,"father":"Abraham","mother":"Sarah","v":[13]}],"places":[{"id":"horeb_576","name":"Horeb","kind":"Church","lat":28.58771,"lon":33.92168,"summary":"Desert or mountain of the dried-up ground, a general name for the whole mountain range of which Sinai was one of the summits (Ex. 3:1; 17:6; 33:6; Ps. 106:19, etc.).","verses":16,"v":[1]},{"id":"moab_815","name":"Moab","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":31.49916,"lon":35.78051,"summary":"The land of Moab (Jer. 48:24), called also the “country of Moab” (Ruth 1:2, 6; 2:6), on the east of Jordan and the Dead Sea, and south of the Arnon (Num. 21:13, 26).","verses":148,"v":[1]},{"id":"egypt_362","name":"Egypt","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":26.4902,"lon":29.8808,"summary":"The land of the Nile and the pyramids, the oldest kingdom of which we have any record, holds a place of great significance in Scripture.","verses":564,"v":[2,16,25]},{"id":"bashan_159","name":"Bashan","kind":"Region","lat":32.80008,"lon":35.9373,"summary":"Light soil, first mentioned in Gen. 14:5, where it is said that Chedorlaomer and his confederates “smote the Rephaim in Ashteroth,” where Og the king of Bashan had his residence.","verses":52,"v":[7]},{"id":"heshbon_565","name":"Heshbon","kind":"City","lat":31.79819,"lon":35.80986,"summary":"Intelligence, a city ruled over by Sihon, king of the Amorites (Josh. 3:10; 13:17). It was taken by Moses (Num. 21:23-26), and became afterwards a Levitical city (Josh. 21:39) in the tribe of Reuben (Num. 32:37).","verses":37,"v":[7]},{"id":"gad_1286","name":"Gad","kind":"Region","lat":32.04697,"lon":35.7458,"summary":"Added from Digital Manna places-1262 (LPF sync 2026-10-13)","verses":21,"v":[8]},{"id":"admah_27","name":"Admah","kind":"City","lat":31.11942,"lon":35.41253,"summary":"Earth, one of the five cities of the vale of Siddim (Gen. 10:19). It was destroyed along with Sodom and Gomorrah (19:24; Deut. 29:23).","verses":5,"v":[23]},{"id":"gomorrah_489","name":"Gomorrah","kind":"City","lat":31.15725,"lon":35.47395,"summary":"Submersion, one of the five cities of the plain of Siddim which were destroyed by fire (Gen. 10:19; 13:10; 19:24, 28). These cities probably stood close together, and were near the northern extremity of what is now the Dead Sea.","verses":23,"v":[23]},{"id":"sodom_1107","name":"Sodom","kind":"City","lat":31.19656,"lon":35.39648,"summary":"Burning; the walled, a city in the vale of Siddim (Gen. 13:10; 14:1-16). The wickedness of its inhabitants brought down upon it fire from heaven, by which it was destroyed (18:16-33; 19:1-29; Deut. 23:17).","verses":47,"v":[23]},{"id":"zeboiim_1244","name":"Zeboiim","kind":"City","lat":31.11942,"lon":35.41253,"summary":"One of the “five cities of the plain” of Sodom, generally coupled with Admah (Gen. 10:19; 14:2; Deut. 29:23; Hos. 11:8). It had a king of its own (Shemeber), and was therefore a place of some importance.","verses":5,"v":[23]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[428,1697,1697,1697,1285,1285,1285,834,3068,3068,6680,4872,3772,3772,854,1121,1121,776,776,776,4124,4124,905,905,905,1285,1285,3772,3772,3772,854,854,2722,2722],[4872,7121,3605,3478,559,559,413,413,